  ],
  "text": "Oil is not mainly fuel. It is plastic, fertiliser, medicine, road surface and most of your clothes. You think of a barrel as petrol. Petrol is only one slice of it. The rest becomes diesel, jet fuel, lubricants, asphalt, and the feedstock for chemicals. Almost every plastic object anywhere near you started out as oil. But the biggest one is the one nobody names. Fertiliser. Plants need nitrogen. The air is nearly four fifths nitrogen and plants cannot touch it. The Haber Bosch process pulls it out of the air, using enormous heat and pressure. That heat comes from fossil fuel. That fertiliser grows about half the world's food. Which means roughly half the nitrogen atoms in your body came through that process. Fossil fuel is not just in your tank. It is in your tissue. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
